# Cloudflare Pages header overrides (read from the deploy root).
#
# The glue JS and the wasm are ONE artifact — wasm-bindgen mangles import
# names with a per-build hash — so any skew between them is fatal:
#
#   LinkError: Import #5 "./digblock_web_bg.js" "__wbg_ready_<hash>":
#   function import requires a callable
#
# This file used to be the whole defence, pinning /pkg/* to `no-cache` against
# Pages' 4-hour default for `.js`. It is NOT sufficient: on a custom domain the
# CDN in front of Pages caches `.js` (a default static extension) under the
# zone's 4h browser TTL and rewrites Cache-Control on the way out, while `.wasm`
# — not a default static extension — passes through with `no-cache` intact. Same
# fatal pairing, one layer further out, and unreachable from here:
#
#   digblock.pages.dev/pkg/digblock_web.js  ->  no-cache       (this file)
#   digblock.net/pkg/digblock_web.js        ->  max-age=14400  (zone override)
#
# So correctness now lives in `just build-web`: both files carry the same build
# stamp in their name, and only index.html knows it. That makes the pair
# immutable by construction, which is what these headers say — any cache, at any
# layer, holding either file forever is now correct behaviour rather than a bug.
/pkg/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
